## Why This Is Asked

Tests for real-time collaboration systems must handle offline edits, eventual consistency, and deterministic merges. This question evaluates your ability to architect an end-to-end flow that exercises offline queues, CRDT-based merging, and version history while ensuring test isolation and reproducibility.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first collaboration with optimistic UI updates
- CRDT-based merge algorithms ensuring deterministic outcomes
- Test data isolation using per-test seeds and unique identifiers
- Server-sync mocks with controlled timing for deterministic test results

## Code Example

```javascript
// Setup two Playwright contexts for concurrent user simulation
const contextA = await browser.newContext();
const contextB = await browser.newContext();
const pageA = await contextA.newPage();
const pageB = await contextB.newPage();

// Seed a shared base document
const docId = await seedDocument({ content: 'Initial paragraph.' });

// Simulate offline for both users
await setNetworkOffline(pageA);
await setNetworkOffline(pageB);

// User A edits the paragraph
await pageA.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageA.locator('.editor').fill('User A edited this.');

// User B edits the same paragraph offline
await pageB.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageB.locator('.editor').fill('User B edited that.');

// Reconnect both users to trigger CRDT sync
await setNetworkOnline(pageA);
await setNetworkOnline(pageB);

// Wait for sync completion
await expect(pageA.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');
await expect(pageB.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');

// Verify idempotent replay
const versionBefore = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
await triggerSyncAgain(pageA);
const versionAfter = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
expect(versionAfter).toBe(versionBefore);

// Verify version history
const history = await getVersionHistory(docId);
expect(history).toContain('User A edited this.');
expect(history).toContain('User B edited that.');
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of end-to-end testing in a complex, multi-region, event-sourced delivery application. It checks whether the candidate can design tests that cover data isolation, cross-region convergence, failure handling, and compliance scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- Event-sourced E2E flows with Kafka domain topics and region-specific read models
- Cross-region consistency and latency budget validation
- Multi-tenant data isolation and DSAR (Data Subject Access Request) compliance
- Fault injection including regional outages and retry mechanisms
- Observability integration and deterministic seed data

## Code Example
```javascript
// Seed deterministic test data and publish events to Kafka; verify read-model convergence
const seedOrder = { id: 'ORD-123', tenantId: 'tenant-acme', region: 'us-east' };

await kafka.publish('orders.us-east', { 
  eventType: 'OrderPlaced', 
  payload: seedOrder, 
  timestamp: '2026-01-15T10:00:00Z' 
});

await kafka.publish('drivers.us-east', {
  eventType: 'DriverAssigned',
  payload: { orderId: 'ORD-123', driverId: 'DRV-456' }
});

// Verify real-time WebSocket delivery to clients
const wsUpdate = await waitForWebSocketMessage('rider-client', 'ETAUpdated');
expect(wsUpdate.payload.eta).toBeWithinSLA();

// Validate cross-region read-model convergence
const readModel = await readModelClient.query('us-west', 'orders', { id: 'ORD-123' });
expect(readModel.status).toEqual('confirmed');
expect(readModel.convergenceTime).toBeLessThan(SLA_THRESHOLD_MS);

// Verify tenant isolation
const crossTenantResult = await readModelClient.query('us-east', 'orders', { 
  id: 'ORD-123', 
  tenantId: 'tenant-foreign' 
});
expect(crossTenantResult.accessDenied).toBe(true);

// DSAR deletion verification
await dsarService.requestDeletion('customer-789');
await waitForEventProcessing();
const piiCheck = await readModelClient.scanAllRegions('customer-789');
expect(piiCheck.found).toBe(false);

// Region failover test
await regionOutageSimulator.failover('us-east', 'us-west');
const failoverState = await readModelClient.getState('us-west', 'ORD-123');
expect(failoverState.reconstructed).toBe(true);
